# Placeholders only, for the owner's Apple Developer Program sitting. Export real values in the shell that runs the build;
# never write them into this file or any note. The Developer ID certificate stays in the Mac's keychain.
APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: <LEGAL NAME> (<TEAM_ID>)"
APPLE_TEAM_ID="<TEAM_ID>"
# Notarisation: the Apple ID and an app-specific password.
APPLE_ID="<APPLE_ID_EMAIL>"
APPLE_PASSWORD="<APP_SPECIFIC_PASSWORD>"
# Updates: `node tools/desktop/updater-key.mjs` made the pair on 24 October. The private key and its password live in
# the keychain, and `tools/desktop/release.mjs` reads them into the build; they are not set here.
# Publishing (`release.mjs --publish`): a Cloudflare API token that may write the R2 bucket braindog-desktop
# (Workers R2 Storage: Edit), and the account it is in. Or leave these out and run `wrangler login` once.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN="<R2_EDIT_TOKEN>"
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID="<ACCOUNT_ID>"
